# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# DEDUCTIVE 404 — example environment configuration
#
# Copy this file to `.env` (git-ignored) and fill in real values, or set the
# same names in Render → Environment. NEVER commit a real connection string.
#
# Local usage with a .env file:
#     node --env-file=.env server/index.js
#     node --env-file=.env server/dev.js
# Render: add each key under Environment (no .env file needed there).
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# MongoDB Atlas — the permanent source of truth for every game, room, case,
# answer, score and per-player timer. When this is set, saved data survives
# server restarts, sleep/wake and redeployments.
#
# Get your free-tier (M0) string from Atlas:
#   cloud.mongodb.com → your project → Database → Connect → Drivers →
#   "Connect your application" → copy the URI, replace <password>, choose a db name.
# Credentials live ONLY in this variable — server-side, never in frontend code.
MONGODB_URI=mongodb+srv://jayaprakashdarkdevil_db_user:bavee123@cluster0.pfcdebe.mongodb.net/?appName=Cluster0

# Optional: database name inside the Atlas cluster (default: deductive404).
# D404_MONGODB_DB=deductive404

# Admin login (game master). Server-side only — never sent to the browser.
# D404_ADMIN_USER=admin
# D404_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-to-a-long-secret

# ── SQL engine (used only when MONGODB_URI is NOT set) ──────────────────────
# Local development defaults to the SQLite file in data/ (no setup needed).
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://user:password@host:5432/dbname

# ── Optional overrides (defaults suit almost every setup) ───────────────────
# D404_DATA_DIR=./data                # sqlite file, uploads, signing secret
# D404_MAX_PLAYERS_PER_ROOM=50        # seat cap per room
# PORT=5175                           # player site; admin uses PORT+1
